Part 1: Proposal for Website Development 

 

Website Topic & Purpose "My website will focus on 'World-Class Travel Destinations,' showcasing iconic locations across different continents. Its purpose is to inspire travelers to explore famous landmarks, cultural hubs, and natural wonders while providing them with helpful travel information."
Intended Audience "The website is designed for travelers of all ages and backgrounds who are planning trips or simply dreaming about their next adventure. Visitors will interact with the site to explore destinations, view travel tips, and access resources for their trips."
Planned Pages & Navigation Structure
index.html (Home): A welcoming page with featured destinations and highlights from different continents. 
history.html: The historical significance of iconic landmarks like the Great Wall of China, the Eiffel Tower, and the Grand Canyon. 
originators.html: Profiles of influential travelers, explorers, or travel influencers who popularized these locations. 
current.html: Travel tips, packing guides, and updates on trending destinations or must-see attractions. 
contact.html: A form for visitors to ask questions, provide feedback, or share travel stories.                                                                                                                                              4. Wireframe Mockups:  Untitled design.png
Color Scheme & Typography Choices "The website will use vibrant colors like blue, green, and white to evoke a sense of adventure and freshness. A modern sans-serif font will be used for headings to keep the design clean, while the body text will use an easy-to-read serif font."
Features & Technologies To make it engage:
Add an interactive map that highlights top destinations when clicked. 
Use a JavaScript-powered slideshow on the homepage for destination images. 
Create a dynamic contact form with dropdown options and input validation. 
As the sole contributor to this project, I will be responsible for all roles involved in website development. This includes: 

Design & Layout: Creating wireframes and defining the visual style, including color scheme and typography. 
Content Creation: Researching and writing content for each of the planned pages. 
Coding & Implementation: Developing the website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, and integrating interactive elements. 
Testing & Debugging: Ensuring the website is functional, user-friendly, and free from errors."* 
